1. SRS Documentation
1.1 Project Overview and Purpose
The Devolenz Software License Management System is a web-based application designed to help organisations manage software licenses efficiently. The system allows administrators to maintain software inventory, assign licenses to employees, monitor license usage, and manage license requests through a centralized platform.
The main purpose of the application is to reduce manual tracking errors, improve visibility of available licenses, and simplify the process of assigning and monitoring software licenses within an organisation.
The application provides role-based functionality for administrators and users. Administrators can add, edit, assign, and delete licenses, while users can request software licenses and monitor assigned licenses.

1.2 Problem Statement and Scope
Problem Statement
Many organisations still manage software licenses manually using spreadsheets or disconnected systems. This creates issues such as:
Difficulty tracking license availability
Risk of expired licenses
Lack of centralized monitoring
Manual approval delays
Increased operational overhead
The proposed system addresses these issues by providing an automated and centralized license management platform.
Project Scope
The project includes:
User authentication and authorization
License management
License request system
User management
License assignment tracking
Cloud deployment using AWS EC2
Load balancing using AWS Application Load Balancer
Monitoring using AWS CloudWatch
Out of Scope
The project does not include:
Integration with external enterprise identity systems
Payment processing
Mobile application support
Advanced analytics dashboard

1.3 User Characteristics
Administrators
IT administrators or software managers
Moderate to advanced technical knowledge
Responsible for managing licenses and users
Require access to monitoring and reporting features
Users
Employees within the organisation
Basic technical knowledge
Can request software licenses
Can monitor assigned licenses
The system was designed with a simple and responsive interface to support users with different technical skill levels.

1.4 Constraints
The following constraints influenced the development of the project:
Technical Constraints
Deployment limited to AWS EC2 Free Tier resources
Application hosted using Ubuntu EC2 instances
Load balancing configured using AWS Application Load Balancer
MongoDB used as the backend database
Business Constraints
Limited project timeline
Team collaboration requirements
Requirement to implement CI/CD pipeline
Security Constraints
JWT-based authentication required
Restricted API access for protected routes
Secure password handling required

1.5 Functional Requirements
ID	Functional Requirement
FR-01	The system shall allow users to register an account.
FR-02	The system shall allow users to login securely.
FR-03	The system shall allow administrators to add software licenses.
FR-04	The system shall allow administrators to edit licenses.
FR-05	The system shall allow administrators to delete licenses.
FR-06	The system shall display all available licenses.
FR-07	The system shall allow users to request licenses.
FR-08	The system shall allow administrators to approve or reject requests.
FR-09	The system shall track assigned licenses.
FR-10	The system shall allow administrators to manage users.
FR-11	The system shall support cloud deployment using AWS.
FR-12	The system shall distribute traffic using load balancing.

1.6 Non-Functional Requirements (NFRs)
ID	Non-Functional Requirement
NFR-01	The system shall respond within 2 seconds under normal load.
NFR-02	The system shall support concurrent user access.
NFR-03	The system shall provide secure authentication using JWT.
NFR-04	The system shall maintain high availability using load balancing.
NFR-05	The system shall support scalability through cloud infrastructure.
NFR-06	The system shall provide maintainable modular code structure.
NFR-07	The user interface shall be responsive and user-friendly.
NFR-08	The system shall maintain data consistency and integrity.

