4. Functional Testing
Functional testing was conducted to validate that all major features of the Devolenz Software License Management System operated according to the specified functional requirements. Testing was performed on both frontend and backend functionalities to ensure correct behavior, user interaction, role-based access control, request processing, and database operations.
The testing process focused on validating:
Authentication and authorization
License management operations
User management functionalities
License request workflow
Role-based navigation
Error handling and validation
Session management
The application was tested using realistic user scenarios involving both administrator and standard user accounts. All core functionalities passed successfully without critical failures.

4.1 Functional Testing Approach
The testing approach involved executing predefined test cases and verifying whether the actual application behavior matched the expected system behavior.
The testing process included:
1.Executing valid and invalid user actions
2.Verifying API responses and frontend behavior
3.Checking database updates after operations
4.Validating access permissions based on user roles
5.Monitoring error handling and validation messages
Testing was conducted after integrating frontend and backend modules to ensure complete end-to-end functionality.

4.2 Functional Test Cases
Test ID	Functionality	Expected Result	Actual Result	Status
FT-01	Admin Login	Admin should login with valid credentials and navigate to admin dashboard	Admin logged in successfully and dashboard displayed	PASS
FT-02	Invalid Login	System should show error for incorrect email or password	Error message displayed: invalid email or password	PASS
FT-03	User Login	User should login with valid credentials and navigate to user dashboard	User logged in successfully and user dashboard displayed	PASS
FT-04	Add License	Admin should be able to add a new software license	New license was added and displayed in the license list	PASS
FT-05	Update License	Admin should be able to edit an existing license	License details were updated successfully	PASS
FT-06	Delete License	Admin should be able to delete a selected license	Selected license was removed from the license list	PASS
FT-07	View All Users	Admin should be able to view registered users	User list displayed with name, email, role and action options	PASS
FT-08	Assign License to User	Admin should be able to assign available license to a user	License was assigned to the selected user	PASS
FT-09	Remove Assigned License	Admin should be able to remove an assigned license from a user	Assigned license was removed successfully	PASS
FT-10	User View Assigned Licenses	User should only view licenses assigned to them	Assigned licenses displayed in user dashboard	PASS
FT-11	Submit Normal License Request	User should be able to submit a normal license request	Request was submitted and displayed with normal priority	PASS
FT-12	Submit Urgent License Request	User should be able to submit urgent request	Request was submitted and priority displayed as high	PASS
FT-13	View License Requests as Admin	Admin should see all user license requests	All pending/processed requests displayed in Requests page	PASS
FT-14	Approve License Request	Admin should approve pending request and assign license automatically	Request status changed to approved and license assigned to user	PASS
FT-15	Reject License Request	Admin should reject pending request	Request status changed to rejected	PASS
FT-16	Prevent Duplicate Assignment	System should prevent assigning same license twice to same user	Error message displayed when duplicate assignment attempted	PASS
FT-17	Prevent Assignment When No Licenses Available	System should prevent assignment when total license limit is reached	Error message displayed: no licenses available	PASS
FT-18	Role-Based Navigation for Admin	Admin should see Licenses, Users, Requests and Logout in navbar	Admin navbar options displayed correctly	PASS
FT-19	Role-Based Navigation for User	User should only see user-related options and Logout	User navbar displayed without admin-only options	PASS
FT-20	Logout	User/admin should logout and return to login page	Session ended and login page displayed	PASS
