6. Load Balancing and Load Testing
6.1 Load Balancer Setup
The application was deployed on two separate AWS EC2 instances to improve reliability and availability. An AWS Application Load Balancer (ALB) was configured to distribute incoming traffic evenly between both servers.
The target group was configured using HTTP protocol with port 3000, and both EC2 instances were registered successfully. Health checks were configured to monitor the application availability.
