8. Discussion and Conclusion
The development of the Devolenz Software License Management System provided valuable experience in full-stack software development, cloud deployment, testing, and DevOps practices.
The project successfully implemented core software engineering concepts including SRS documentation, design patterns, object-oriented programming principles, API testing, CI/CD pipeline integration, and cloud infrastructure deployment.
AWS services such as EC2, Application Load Balancer, and CloudWatch significantly improved the reliability and scalability of the system. The implementation of load balancing demonstrated how cloud-based architectures can improve availability and fault tolerance.
Throughout the project, the team faced challenges related to deployment configuration, load balancing setup, target group health checks, and environment management. These challenges improved the team’s understanding of cloud networking, application deployment, and infrastructure monitoring.
In conclusion, the project achieved its intended objectives by delivering a functional and scalable software license management system with cloud-based deployment and monitoring capabilities.

9. Reflection
This project provided significant practical experience in software development, cloud deployment, testing, and team collaboration. One of the most valuable lessons learned was how different software engineering concepts integrate together in a real-world application.
The implementation of AWS services such as EC2, Load Balancer, and CloudWatch improved understanding of cloud infrastructure and system scalability. Configuring target groups, managing security groups, and troubleshooting health checks provided hands-on experience with cloud networking concepts.
The project also strengthened knowledge of CI/CD pipelines and deployment automation using GitHub Actions and PM2. Team collaboration through GitHub branches, pull requests, and merge conflict resolution improved version control and collaborative development skills.
Several technical difficulties were encountered during development. These included API connection issues, load balancer timeout errors, target group health check failures, and frontend/backend deployment synchronization problems. Resolving these issues required extensive debugging, testing, and infrastructure configuration.
Additionally, the project improved problem-solving skills, communication skills, and understanding of software project management processes. Overall, the project was a valuable learning experience that combined theoretical knowledge with practical implementation.

